#{[17592186556994 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186556994 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186556994 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e442d8f5-617c-59ab-a4ac-822779b6d576" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557128 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186556539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557128 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186556805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557128 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186556869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557128 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186556878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557128 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186556994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557128 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557128 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557128 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186556878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557128 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6dce9295-adc4-54f0-85bb-a7daa031279d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557327 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557327 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163156" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557327 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557327 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f(x,y)$ and the region $D$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=6xy,\\,D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 4x\\}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that the volume of the solid enclosed between the surface $z=f(x,y)$ and the $xy$-plane over the region $D$ equals the volume of the right cylinder with base $D$ and height $f(a,b).$ Find $a$ given that $b=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557327 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f6236dff-5836-5e2b-be74-a41334b247e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557327 #edb/ref 1074 "According to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=f(a,b)\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral on the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}(6xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4x}6xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[3x{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}48{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[12{x}^{4}]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4x}\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[y]_{y=0}^{y=4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we are told that $b=2.$ So, our initial equation simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =f(a,2)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 12 & =(6a\\cdot 2)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 12 & =24a \\\\ a & =\\frac{12}{24} \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $(\\frac{1}{2},2)\\in D.$ Therefore, the answer is $a=\\frac{1}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557348 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186557372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557348 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2fdac4bf-88bd-5b8c-8156-abdd95028924" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557348 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186167133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557369 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186557348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557369 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "76a6bdfb-b2d3-5c1f-94fe-835169048009" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557369 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186167132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557372 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186557383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557372 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "837149fd-427b-5257-8438-799b8410b152" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557372 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186557327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557383 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186557390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557383 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "99580cac-da4a-5eeb-8345-69ac73a2ebdf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557383 #edb/ref 1063